@page "/"

<PageTitle>RevalQuery with MudBlazor</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">RevalQuery with MudBlazor</MudText>

<MudText Class="mb-4">
    A standalone WebAssembly app. Everything RevalQuery needs here is one call to
    <MudChip T="string" Size="Size.Small">AddRevalQuery()</MudChip> in Program.cs and
    <MudChip T="string" Size="Size.Small">@("<QueryHost Scope=\"Q\" />")</MudChip> on any
    page that queries.
</MudText>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h6" GutterBottom="true">Where the two libraries meet</MudText>

<MudList T="string" Class="mb-4">
    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.TableChart" Href="products">
        <MudText><b>Table and detail.</b> A query's IsLoading drives MudTable's Loading, and
        picking a row enables a second query that was disabled until then.</MudText>
    </MudListItem>
    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Search" Href="autocomplete">
        <MudText><b>Autocomplete.</b> MudAutocomplete wants a search function, not a render
        loop, so this one goes through QueryAsync and gets the cache for free.</MudText>
    </MudListItem>
    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.RateReview" Href="reviews">
        <MudText><b>Form and mutation.</b> A MudForm posts through Q.Mutation, then
        invalidates the query that reads the list back.</MudText>
    </MudListItem>
</MudList>

<MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" Variant="Variant.Outlined">
    Every handler here waits between half a second and a second on purpose. The point of the
    pages is what the UI does while it waits, and what it does not do on a second visit.
</MudAlert>
